Give OHOS the strings the OS-level geolocation bubble needs.

ohos-system-geolocation-permission.patch turns on
os_level_geolocation_permission_supported for OHOS. That flag also gates
ContentSettingGeolocationBubbleModel::InitializeSystemGeolocationPermissionBubble(),
which does not build on a platform the flag did not previously cover:

  content_setting_bubble_model.cc:1482:33: error: use of undeclared identifier 'IDS_TURNED_OFF'
  content_setting_bubble_model.cc:1484:50: error: use of undeclared identifier 'IDS_OPEN_SETTINGS_LINK'

IDS_TURNED_OFF, IDS_OPEN_SETTINGS_LINK and IDS_GEOLOCATION_TURNED_OFF_IN_OS
live inside <if expr="is_macosx or is_chromeos or is_win"> in
generated_resources.grd -- exactly the three platforms the flag used to name.
OHOS is added to those conditions. grit has no "ohos" platform and this port
maps it to the Linux resource set (tools/grit/grit_args.gni), but the build
already passes an is_ohos define and chromium_strings.grd already tests it, so
the expression works.

The second half is not a build error and matters more. The function picks its
title with

  #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
    set_title(...);
  #else
    NOTREACHED();
  #endif

whose #else assumes the only other platform reaching here is Linux, where the
flag is off. With the flag on for OHOS that NOTREACHED() becomes live, and this
build compiles NOTREACHED() to a trap: opening the content-settings bubble for
a site whose geolocation is blocked at the OS level would kill the browser.
That is the same shape as the Web Serial and GlobalAcceleratorListener traps
already fixed on this branch -- an unimplemented-platform marker that the port
makes reachable. OHOS joins the arm that sets a title.

Found by building the patch on the runner; it does not compile without this.

diff --git a/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd b/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
index d718a56fe4..ee40cdd3cf 100644
--- a/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
+++ b/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
@@ -16182,7 +16182,7 @@ Please help our engineers fix this problem. Tell us what happened right before y
       <message name="IDS_GEOLOCATION_WILL_ASK_AGAIN" desc="Info message that tells user that the website will prompt for geolocation permission again next time">
           This site will ask again next time.
       </message>
-      <if expr="is_macosx or is_chromeos or is_win">
+      <if expr="is_macosx or is_chromeos or is_win or is_ohos">
         <message name="IDS_GEOLOCATION_TURNED_OFF_IN_OS" desc="Title for the geolocation bubble that is used when a site requests geolocation, but geolocation is blocked on an OS level.">
           Location is turned off in system settings
         </message>
@@ -16283,7 +16283,7 @@ Please help our engineers fix this problem. Tell us what happened right before y
           Microphone turned off
         </message>
       </if>
-      <if expr="is_macosx or is_chromeos or is_win">
+      <if expr="is_macosx or is_chromeos or is_win or is_ohos">
         <message name="IDS_TURNED_OFF" desc="Description text for the state of camera or microphone or geolocation">
           Turned off
         </message>
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/content_settings/content_setting_bubble_model.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/content_settings/content_setting_bubble_model.cc
index 046bc71d81..e01559978d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/content_settings/content_setting_bubble_model.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/content_settings/content_setting_bubble_model.cc
@@ -1467,7 +1467,8 @@ void ContentSettingGeolocationBubbleModel::CommitChanges() {
 void ContentSettingGeolocationBubbleModel::
     InitializeSystemGeolocationPermissionBubble() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(OS_LEVEL_GEOLOCATION_PERMISSION_SUPPORTED)
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
+    BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
   set_title(l10n_util::GetStringUTF16(IDS_GEOLOCATION_TURNED_OFF_IN_OS));
 #else
   // The system-level location permission is not supported on Linux.
